## View Implementation

- Use HookConsumerWidget
- Watch state with ref.watch
- Handle loading/errors
- Validate inputs
- Implement proper auth flow
- Use custom hooks for lifecycle management

## Custom Hooks for Screen Lifecycle

1. Screen Lifecycle Management: 
   Use the appropriate hooks for managing different aspects of screen lifecycle:

   ```dart
   // 1. Handle screen focus (when returning from another screen)
   final focusNode = useScreenFocus(
     ref,
     isRefreshing: isRefreshing,
     onFocusGained: () => viewModel.refreshData(),
   );
   
   // 2. Handle app lifecycle (background/foreground transitions)
   useAppLifecycle(
     ref,
     isRefreshing: isRefreshing,
     onResumeFromBackground: () => viewModel.resubscribeToSources(),
   );
   
   // 3. Handle initial data loading
   useInitialLoad(ref, onLoad: () {
     viewModel.fetchInitialData();
   });
   
   // 4. Use the focusNode in your Focus widget
   return Focus(
     focusNode: focusNode,
     autofocus: true,
     child: YourScreenContent(),
   );
   ```

2. When to use each hook:
   - `useScreenFocus`: When the screen needs to refresh data after navigation
   - `useAppLifecycle`: When the screen manages connections (WebSockets, streams) that need handling on app background/foreground
   - `useInitialLoad`: For initial data loading when the screen mounts
   - All screens should share a common state variable for tracking refresh operations

3. Shared Refresh State Pattern:
   ```dart
   // At the beginning of your build method:
   final isRefreshing = useState(false);
   
   // Share this state between hooks to prevent duplicate refreshes
   ```

## Color Usage

1. Opacity:
   - Use `withValues(alpha: value)` instead of deprecated `withOpacity(value)`
   - Example: `Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.1)` instead of `Colors.black.withOpacity(0.1)`
   - Alpha values should be between 0 and 1 (0.1 opacity = .1 alpha)

### Example View:
```dart
class AuthWrapper extends HookConsumerWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    final authState = ref.watch(authServiceProvider);
    final profileState = ref.watch(profileViewModelProvider);
    final isRefreshing = useState(false);
    
    // Handle app lifecycle
    useAppLifecycle(
      ref,
      isRefreshing: isRefreshing,
      onResumeFromBackground: () => ref.read(authServiceProvider.notifier).refreshToken(),
    );
    
    // Handle initial load
    useInitialLoad(ref, onLoad: () {
      if (authState.hasValue && authState.value != AuthType.none) {
        ref.read(profileViewModelProvider.notifier).getUserProfile();
      }
    });

    // Handle loading state
    if (authState.isLoading || profileState.isLoading) {
      return const LoadingScreen();
    }

    // Handle profile status based on auth type
    if (profileState.profile != null) {
      switch (profileState.profile!.status) {
        case ProfileStatus.approved:
          return const HomeScreen();
        case ProfileStatus.pending:
          return const PendingApprovalScreen();
        case ProfileStatus.rejected:
          return const RejectedScreen();
        case ProfileStatus.block:
          return const BlockedScreen();
      }
    }

    return const LoginScreen();
  }
}
```

## Form Handling

1. Form Controllers:
```dart
// Using useMemoized for controllers
final controllers = useMemoized(
  () => {
    'email': TextEditingController(),
    'password': TextEditingController(),
  },
  const [],
);

// Dispose controllers
useEffect(() {
  return () {
    for (final controller in controllers.values) {
      controller.dispose();
    }
  };
}, const []);
```

2. Input Validation:
```dart
// Phone number
FilteringTextInputFormatter.digitsOnly,
LengthLimitingTextInputFormatter(10),

// Date formatter
TextInputFormatter dateFormatter() {
  return TextInputFormatter.withFunction((oldValue, newValue) {
    var text = newValue.text;
    if (text.length > 8) return oldValue;
    text = text.replaceAll(RegExp(r'[^\d]'), '');
    if (text.length >= 2) {
      text = '${text.substring(0, 2)}/${text.substring(2)}';
    }
    if (text.length >= 5) {
      text = '${text.substring(0, 5)}/${text.substring(5)}';
    }
    return TextEditingValue(
      text: text,
      selection: TextSelection.collapsed(offset: text.length),
    );
  });
}
```

3. Color Management

- Use `withValues(alpha: value)` instead of `withOpacity(value)` for opacity adjustments
- `withOpacity()` is deprecated and should be avoided
- Ensure consistent color opacity throughout the app
- Example:

```dart
// Correct approach
BoxShadow(
  color: Colors.black.withValues(alpha: 0.25),
  blurRadius: 10,
)

// Incorrect approach (deprecated)
BoxShadow(
  color: Colors.black.withOpacity(0.25),
  blurRadius: 10,
)
```

## UI Feedback

1. Success Messages:
   - Green color (CAF50)
   - Auto-dismiss after 8s
   - Clear action description

2. Error Messages:
   - Red color (64238)
   - Auto-dismiss after 8s
   - User-friendly error description
   - Actionable solution when possible

3. Loading States:
   - Show progress indicators
   - Disable interactions
   - Maintain UI consistency

## Asset Management

1. Flutter Assets Generator:
   - Always run `fluttergen -c ./pubspec.yaml` after adding any new assets
   - Command regenerates the asset references in `lib/core/constants/assets.gen.dart`

2. Referencing Assets:
   - Use generated asset references instead of string paths
   - Example: `IndikoshAssets.svg.flightVector.path` instead of 'assets/svg/flight_vector.svg'
   - Benefits:
     - Type-safe access
     - Compile-time validation
     - Auto-completion support
     - Prevents typos and missing asset errors

3. Example Asset Usage:
```dart
// Correct approach (using generated assets)
SvgPicture.asset(
  IndikoshAssets.svg.flightVector.path,
  width: 24.w,
  height: 24.h,
)

// Incorrect approach (using string paths)
SvgPicture.asset(
  'assets/svg/flight_vector.svg',
  width: 24.w,
  height: 24.h,
)
```